%description:
The cells of a site share one LOS state, one environment height and one shadowing realization
towards a UE, which are drawn for one position of the site. Two sectors on one mast whose
antennas are 3 m apart in height would share a realization drawn at the position of one of them,
and a link moved more than the correlation distance since the last draw is drawn again: in an
Indoor Factory hall (DL, DH: 1 m) at every switch between the sectors, and the shadowing is
decorrelated by the height difference in every scenario. That is an error at initialization, as
for sectors apart horizontally (SiteRejected_SectorsApart).

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: test.ned
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth10G;
import simu5g.nodes.gNodeB;
import simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork;

network TwoSectorTestNetwork extends NrSessionTestNetwork
{
    submodules:
        gnb2: gNodeB {
            @display("p=650,250");
        }
    connections:
        upf.pppg++ <--> Eth10G <--> gnb2.ppp;
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = TwoSectorTestNetwork

*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1

# two sectors on one mast
*.gnb*.cellularNic.radio.site = "mast"
*.gnb*.cellularNic.antenna.txDirection = "ANISOTROPIC"
*.gnb.cellularNic.antenna.txAngle = 60deg
*.gnb2.cellularNic.antenna.txAngle = 180deg
**.dynamicLos = true
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 450m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb2.cellularNic.antenna.mobility.offsetZ = 28m
# 28 m is outside TR 38.901 UMa's "hBS=25m"; the check of a link's heights is not what this tests
**.nrChannelModel[*].tolerateHeightViolation = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
the cells of the site 'mast' are not at one place: the antennas of nodes 1 and 2 are 3 m apart.
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
